  "method": "cuda.Event timing, best-of-30 after 10 warmup iters PER TRIAL, 15 independent trials per implementation in round-robin order (not blocked per implementation) to spread thermal/clock drift evenly, median across trials reported. reference.py runs fp32 on GPU (per-batch Python loop); kernels run fp16 (single fused kernel over the whole batch, v4 = phase1+phase2). Not a dtype-matched comparison \u2014 each implementation in its natural/enforced dtype. v2/v3/v4 use block_n=128 (v1 has no block_n knob; its tile is fixed to page_size); v3 additionally pins num_stages=4; v4 uses num_splits=16 (from bench_v4_num_splits.py's sweep at batch=1). cuda_v1 is a raw CUDA C++ extension (torch.utils.cpp_extension JIT), grid=(batch, num_kv_heads) same as Triton v1 but token-by-token dot products, each GQA row running its own independent block-wide shared-memory tree reduction (see cuda/kernel_v1_naive.cu) \u2014 a deliberately more naive baseline than Triton v1, not a tuned competitor. cuda_v2 batches that reduction across all GQA rows into one shared-memory tile per token instead of one reduction per row (see cuda/kernel_v2_shared_tile.cu), the padded (production) variant."
